Z||000000||petealft||07-07-99||11:13 AM||||just bought 85 SE, getting no fuel to injectors.  engine light does not come on. is there any relation to the above problem, and how do I fix<br>
Z||000001||Cooter||07-07-99||06:48 PM||||First, check to see if the check engine bulb is any good- swap in one that is working and see if it was a blown bulb. Then check all fuses inside the car and fusible links around the battery. There are fuel pump relays on the left side firewall- take out the vent to get a better view of them. They should "click" when the ignition is turned on and click again after about 3 seconds- indicates the pump turning on and off. If nothing is happening at the relays, make sure you are getting power to them, a shop manual will be handy here. Hopefully "Theogre" will read your message and offer some advice because this is all i know to tell you.
Z||000002||petealft||07-08-99||06:24 AM||||cooder, the bulb and fuses are good and fuel pump works.  I'll have a look for bad conections and let ya know. thanks.
Z||000003||DJRice||07-09-99||07:22 AM||||Did you try pulling the fuel line from the TBI and make sure that when you turn the key on that gas actually flows that far up.  This will sound kind of silly but I had the engine out of my 84 for several weeks and when I put it back in, It wouldnt start.  It turns out that some bugs had set up a nest in my fuel line and plugged it quite nicely.<br>
Z||000004||petealft||07-16-99||06:00 AM||||not getting "click" from relays. I'd like to plug in code reader but engine light still does not come on.  I recently looked at a electonic scimatic in a Hayns repare book, and it was very uninformative about the conection. It apears to me that it runs from fuse box to engine light to the fuel injectors. think I should inspect F.I.,or look for a short along the way?
Z||000005||DJRice||07-16-99||07:12 AM||||You could try to "hotwire" the fuel pump.  There is a 3 wire connector that is very close to where the wiring harnesses pass through the firewall to the cabin.  It will have a black, pink, and tan wire.  I was having a problem with the 84 Im working on so I ran wires from the battery to this connector and the pump started up.  That will at least tell you if you need a fuel pump or not.  The black is the ground, and the tan is the hot wire. The pink is the feed for your gas gauge.  Double check that with your haynes manual because I am at work and dont have my book.<p>IF this fixes the problem than you either have a bad ECM, relay, or wiring.  Its probably not the ECM or wiring, unless this is a car that was worked on by those members of the population who have absolutely no clue  what they are doing.
Z||000006||DJRice||07-16-99||07:17 AM||||Ok something else just occured to me.  Has this car ever worked since you bought it?  When you turn the key on but dont start the engine, does the "service engine" light come on at all?  It should stay lit, along with the temp and charge light, until the engine is actually started.  If not then there is a problem with the ECM.  If that engine light does not come on at all, and you have verified that the light works, then the computer is not turning on the Fuel pump, and it is also not firing the injector.  
Z||000007||Kage86GT4SP||07-16-99||11:30 PM||||My other car is having this EXACT same problem.<p>It's an 86 TA with a 383 (stroked 350) TPI and a 700R4.<p>SES light doesn't come on at all; can't run the codes; injectors... welll... don't.  I ran 12 volts to the fuel pump, and have lots of pressure at the Schrader valve.<p>Have spark as well, but nothing at the injectors.<p>I said the heck with it, and ordered another ECM (fortunately, only $93) and so, when I install it, I'll immediately post here to let you all know.<p>K.
Z||000008||petealft||07-19-99||06:22 AM||||all ready hotwired pump, and she is good.  As far as I know the "check engine" light never came on when I bought it. We ran the engin with quick start so I dont think its a ecm.  On sunday I pulled out the Idle air controle, or whatever its called, to see if it was cloged. The pin would not move at all so I tried to take it apart to clean it.  It broke sadly so Im going to replace it. Hopefully this will fire the engine up.
